# 5. SPATIAL REFLOW & COLLISION ENGINE

The repository implements a 2D bounding box collision detection engine with interactive block pushing and upward gravity compaction.

## Bounding Box Collision (`collides`)
```javascript
const collides = (b1, b2) => {
  if (b1.id === b2.id) return false;
  return (
    b1.x < b2.x + b2.w &&
    b1.x + b1.w > b2.x &&
    b1.y < b2.y + b2.h &&
    b1.y + b1.h > b2.y
  );
};
```

## Layout Resolution Engine (`resolveLayout`)
When a block moves or resizes, `resolveLayout(blocks, movingBlock, applyGravity)` resolves collisions:

```text
Step 1: Sort all blocks by Y ascending, then X ascending.
Step 2: Reserve the position of movingBlock in the resolved list.
Step 3: Iterate through sorted non-moving blocks.
        If a block collides with any already-placed block in resolved, increment block.y by 1 
        repeatedly until no collision remains.
Step 4: If applyGravity (Auto-Compact Mode) is TRUE:
        Iterate sorted resolved blocks from top to bottom.
        Attempt to decrement targetBlock.y by 1 recursively until a collision occurs, 
        then step back down by 1.
```

