# 8. RESIZE BEHAVIOR & 4-HANDLE ENGINE

Resizing uses **4 edge handles** (`top`, `bottom`, `left`, `right`).

```text
       ┌───────────── Top Handle ─────────────┐
       │                                      │
 Left Handle                              Right Handle
       │                                      │
       └──────────── Bottom Handle ───────────┘
```

## Edge Handle Specific Behavior

| Handle | Drag Direction | Fixed Edge | Changing Properties | Limits & Snapping |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Right** | Horizontal | Left edge fixed | `width` increases/decreases | `snapW = round((width+gap)/colWidth)`, `1 <= snapW <= 4 - block.x` |
| **Left** | Horizontal | Right edge fixed | `left` & `width` change | `snapX` moves between `0` and `block.x + block.w - 1`; `snapW = initialRight - snapX` |
| **Bottom**| Vertical | Top edge fixed | `height` increases/decreases | `snapH = round((height+gap)/rowHeight)`, `snapH >= 1` |
| **Top** | Vertical | Bottom edge fixed | `top` & `height` change | `snapY` moves between `0` and `block.y + block.h - 1`; `snapH = initialBottom - snapY` |

## Live Collision during Resize
As handles are pulled, `handlePointerMoveResize` recalculates `snapW`, `snapH`, `snapX`, `snapY` and runs `resolveLayout()` continuously so adjacent cards push out of the way in real-time.

